WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.746
Good preparation makes planting, weeding and harvesting easier.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.412
First, clear the site of bush, stumps and large stones.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.783
Next, mark planting rows, so your plants are evenly spaced.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:19.021
Then make mounds or ridges. They help water drain, and make the roots easier to harvest.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:24.415
On loose, well-drained soil, cassava can also be planted on flat land.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:31.682
Before you move on, check: Clear the site. Mark planting rows. Prepare mounds or ridges.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.174
In the next lesson: Planting your cuttings.
